    "heightBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSMway866090450/Q910124 matches current main35185238179282. Current nave part35185238179280 is41m; choir and apse parts35185238179279/278 are37m, with no min_height. Treat these as approximate complete roof envelopes, not stacked solids: estimated nave eave24m/ridge41m and choir eave24m/ridge37m. Retained unqualified65m Wikidata height guides the single clock tower and finial; its masonry44.5m/crown subdivisions are picture estimates. Retained89m length/38m width claims are not used to rescale the unscaled81.4x26.1m mapped church footprint.",
    "scope": "Individual Black Church in Brasov: long gray-tan ashlar Gothic hall with very steep muted red-brown tiled nave roof, lower polygonal eastern choir roof, stepped buttresses, tall pointed recessed glazing and sparse tracery. One tall southwest square clock tower with layered tiled hip/octagonal gallery/spire and slender metal tip, lower northwest corner roof, small south stair turret and small nave ridge fleche. Common shared masonry/tile/wood/metal; mapped footprint and standard-terrain footings. Exact clock mural/numerals, carved sculpture/inscriptions, interiors, trees/neighbor buildings and certified walking excluded."
